course: dictionary
lesson: 12566
title: Calm and proud: dignified
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Dignified describes someone who stays calm, serious and proud, so others respect them. It can also describe something grand and important-looking. When you meet it, look at the words around it. Clues like calm, proud, respect or grand tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «Even when the crowd jeered, the speaker answered in a calm, dignified way.» The crowd was rude, but the speaker did not shout back. The clue is calm, so dignified must mean calm and respectful, even when it is hard.
explain: Dignified can also describe a place or thing. «The dignified old town hall stood tall above the square.» Tall and old tell you it looked grand and important. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Dignified means calm, serious and behaving in a way that makes people respect you.
fact: Dignified can also mean looking important and grand, like «a dignified old building».
fact: A «dignified silence» is a calm, proud silence, where someone does not shout or complain.
fact: Dignity is the noun: to treat someone «with dignity» is to treat them with respect, even when they are in a difficult situation.
fact: Clue words for dignified include calm, proud, respect, serious and grand.
exercise: «Even when the crowd jeered, the speaker answered in a calm, dignified way.» What does dignified mean here? | Fast and hurried | Loud and angry | *Calm, serious and respectful | Silly and funny
exercise: «The dignified old church stood tall above the town.» Find and copy one word in this sentence that means grand and important-looking. | town | *dignified | above | stood
exercise: Grandma says, «We will treat Grandad with dignity, even when he is ill.» What does with dignity mean? | *With respect and calm care | In a hurry to finish | With lots of noise | Very quickly and carelessly
test: «She gave a dignified response, and nobody could say a cross word.» What does a dignified response show? | Boredom and tiredness | Silliness | *Calm self-respect and proper behaviour | Anger and shouting
test: Which phrase means a calm, proud silence? | a noisy party | a loud cheer | *a dignified silence | a cold breeze
exam: Ravi wants to describe a grand old town hall that looks important. Which word fits best? | noisy | *dignified | cheap | tiny
